  "name": "Pitched log-tom rolls",
  "desc": "Synthesized pitched toms with a penv down-glide give a mini log-drum roll in the percussion slot. Two euclid(3,8) tom voices (d3 and a2) rotate their onsets in opposite directions over four cycles while their pans breathe on opposite-phase sweeps; peak adds a third high tom in 5,8 with masked fills. Reichian rolling motion, tuned to D.",
